WEBVTT

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.790
Is that any fun--
crouching in a corner like that?

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.790
Crouching won't change anything.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.250
Stand up and face forward.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.120
Thank you.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.950
For scolding me.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:17.700
I'll never forget what happened today.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:58.870
Yay!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.790
Three, two, one, bye-bye!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.750
Great... Their smiles are so wonderful!

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:36.830
It was such a great idea to spend
our precious holiday on this, Brother!

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:43.410
Yeah. They're all such a great help
at work, this is a good break.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.290
Especially Cacao--she's still a kitten.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.870
She should get some time outside.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.830
Cacao.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.830
You have cream on your face.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:58.120
Chocola.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.910
Hmm, what?

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.080
You have cream on your face.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.790
What next?

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.330
That one.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.200
"Haunted House"

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.120
"Death"

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.790
Was the haunted house that scary?

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.910
You really are easy to scare, aren't you?

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:28.330
Wh-What? I'm not scared at all.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.040
I have to act scared,
otherwise I feel bad for the ghosts.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:37.040
Says the one who has to leave
the bathroom door open at night.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:42.410
You have to keep the fact that May-<i>chan</i>
spreads wide open at night a secret.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:46.000
Hey, stop phrasing it weirdly! You idiot!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.000
So no denial...?

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Maple is still easily scared.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.250
Yes, truly...

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.080
I need to pee.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.500
Oh, the restroom?

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.790
Oh, there it is!

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.160
Okay, let's go.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.160
They seem to be getting along.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.450
Chocola is settling into the big sister role.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.040
I find that quite <i>moe </i>as well.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.620
Oh, what a relief.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.620
Thanks for waiting, everyone!

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.040
Hmm? Where's Cacao?

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.080
Huh?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.950
Oh, no! I-Is she lost?!

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.370
Where did she go?!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:42.200
Chocola, over there.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.160
Oh, there she is!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.700
Come on, you can't wander off like that!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.000
You want to watch this?

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:57.080
Look May-<i>chan</i>! It's <i>Cat Witches</i>!

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.040
I haven't seen that in a while!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.910
Is that the anime from when you
were both kittens? It's still on?

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.160
It's a popular show.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.160
The one that Maple and Cinnamon were
watching was the first in the series.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.200
I think the current one is the third generation.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.790
I see. So it must be very different.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:20.700
Oh, but the opening theme song
is still the same as before!

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.950
I see...

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.950
My dream is to become a singer!

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:29.870
I swear I'll make it come true when I grow up!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:37.080
Oh, no! They've both been captured!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.790
Now how are we going
to rescue the captured kitty?!

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.290
This is really, really bad!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.370
Oh, no!

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.540
Wait, what is she doing?!

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.450
What?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:55.330
Did you miss how she enthusiastically
volunteered to be taken hostage?

00:06:55.330 --> 00:07:00.200
Oh, s-someone, please save me!

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.660
Otherwise, I'm going to get moist!

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.040
Wow, she's really getting into it.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.290
We need the power of song
to save the kitty!

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:17.330
Who in the audience has the courage
to sing at the top of their voices?!

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.870
Why is nobody raising their hands?

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.700
Kids these days are very shy.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.540
Help!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:43.620
That American Curl cat over there!

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:49.040
That cool, elder-sister-posing,
but actually easily scared, <i>tsundere </i>cat!

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.120
Hey, you're up.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.370
Huh?! Why should I...?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:08:01.290
If you help me, I'll keep that thing
that happened a secret!

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.250
That thing?

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.870
Earlier at the haunted house,
you were so scared that you peed--

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:11.620
Hey! What are you trying
to reveal to the public?!

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:17.160
Fine, I'll go! I'll sing, I'll sing!

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.700
Ugh, why me...?

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.330
Sorry, May-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.500
You should be!

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:33.120
Fine, I'm all in... I'll just sing my best...!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:42.410
♪ One flight on a broom, in the dark night ♪

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:48.830
♪ Deliver many stars to you, so just sit tight ♪

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:56.290
♪ A secret spell, let's cast it together ♪

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:01.910
♪ Meow! Two! Three! It's magical for you ♪

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.700
Great... That's great!
I totally got lost in her singing!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.700
I was super impressed, too!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.200
Good stuff!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.830
Truly the pride of the Minaduki family.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.790
I got the best picture imaginable...!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:35.410
Wow, so great! Such a great voice!

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:39.870
Huh? Um, uh... Um?!

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:43.830
Uh... Th-Thank... you.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.540
Wow, we enjoyed everything
there was to enjoy!

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.080
Yes, we truly enjoyed it to the core.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.450
It really was fun.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.790
Especially since I got to hear May-<i>chan</i>'s
singing for the first time in a while!

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:18.000
Okay, it's time. I'm taking off.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.040
Good work!

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.660
Oh, hey, May-<i>chan</i>, wait up!

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.790
I'm home.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.910
You were out late, May-<i>chan</i>.
Where were you?

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:30.160
None of your business.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.620
Oh, I'm so hungry.

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.040
May-<i>chan</i>...?

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:41.160
Yes... Yes, I'll be fine.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.700
So, at that time...

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.290
I'm taking off!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.500
Good work.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.370
Thank you!

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:55.580
Yeah.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.370
Good work, both of you!

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:06.250
Private phone calls, lack of sleep,
sneaking off somewhere...

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.250
This is suspicious.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.450
I'm worried. I can't leave this alone!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.830
Huh? What? May-<i>chan</i>?!

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:23.200
M-May-<i>chan</i>, what could you
possibly be doing out here?!

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.750
C-Could it be...?!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:33.250
N-No, May-<i>chan</i>! That's too adult a profession...

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.040
I totally do want to see
what that'll be like,

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.250
--but, no!
--Cinnamon?

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:41.160
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.830
N-No!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:49.450
I wasn't following you around secretly
because I was worried about you!

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.330
Part-time job?

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:56.700
Oh, but, um... It wasn't like
an indecent job or anything like that.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:00.910
"Yamaneko Musical Instruments"
It was 100% a healthy
and legitimate business.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:05.500
If a customer really wants to,
she would let them touch just a little,

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:10.250
and for first-time customers, she would
teach them the ropes very closely...

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:15.250
She just started but is already
helping other people out, and...

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:19.410
Stop it! How are you able
to make everything sound raunchy?

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.580
What?! No!

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:25.660
But why were you working
at a music store anyway?

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:29.620
Don't we already buy you
everything you need?

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:31.410
That's...

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:36.540
That's because I want to become a singer!

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.290
May-<i>chan</i>...

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:42.950
So I did some research, and I saw that
learning an instrument is a good way

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:46.370
to get started on learning how to sing well.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.250
That's why I wanted to make
some money to buy a guitar.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.370
A guitar?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:57.450
I thought it would be good to learn
an instrument I could play while singing.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.870
That could be an entire
performance by myself.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:03.290
I see. Well, why didn't you just say so?

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:05.660
--Yes, we could just buy you a guitar--

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.080
--That defeats the purpose.
--Yes, we could just buy you a guitar--

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:11.950
Buying the guitar would be the first step
to making my dream come true!

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:13.450
I have to do it myself!

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.370
Maple...

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:19.330
Yeah, I understand how you feel.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:24.040
After all, I'm the guy that jumped out
of the house to start my own shop.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:25.540
Brother...

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.000
Oh, right.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.120
I think I saw it over here...

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.450
Oh, here it is.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.000
"When: July 13th, 12:00 PM
Where: Kanagawa Great Hall"
"Prize: White Guitar!!"
Why don't you try this out?

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.870
"Singing Contest In Kanagawa"
"Contestants Wanted"
Singing contest?

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:44.250
""Prize: White Guitar!!"
If you really want to be a singer,
this would be a good test, too.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.000
Good work, May-<i>chan</i>!

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:04.450
Isn't this tough to do
in addition to the work at home?

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:10.540
Stamina is key to everything. This is
only the beginning--I can't complain.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:13.620
You really are working hard.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.450
Why were you blowing into plastic bottles

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:20.370
and doing that thing with your legs?

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:25.790
Oh, that. It trains my lung capacity
and abdominal breathing techniques.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.580
I see... Oh, I know!

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:31.450
Since you're going to sing
the <i>Cat Witches </i>theme,

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.700
why don't you sing in cosplay?

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.000
Impossible. That outfit is
from when we were kittens.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.290
There's no way I could wear that.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.330
It'll be fine--I can adjust it.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:44.870
No, I won't wear it no matter what.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:49.330
Oh, come on. I wanted to help you.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.450
Don't bother. I never asked for help.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:57.620
I'm doing this because
I want to! Don't worry!

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.870
"Voice & Training Channel"
"Voice Training Tip #1
Mind your facial muscles,
and raise up the tips of your mouth!"

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.330
The big day is here!

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.540
B-Bathroom!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:30.500
O-One more time!

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.910
Again?!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.870
Are you sure you're okay?
Don't pee yourself on stage!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:41.540
P-Pee?! I'd never do that--
I'm not a kitten anymore!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.950
We'll let Cinnamon
take care of you backstage,

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:46.370
but we'll all be cheering
for you at the venue!

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.540
Huh? All of you?

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:52.500
But Kashou, Chocola, and Vanilla
have work to do, right?

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:57.290
He's taking time off for this
special occasion. You're in luck, Maple.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.830
Huh...? Wh-Why...?

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:02.700
For me? There's no need for that.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:06.540
What are you talking about?
It's our precious child's big day.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:10.160
I must engrave the memory in my eyes,
or else I would regret this forever.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:14.330
Of course, I will be recording a video
and uploading to my blog!

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:21.500
Here we are again, the annual
singing contest "Song Paradise!"

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:26.790
We have local bands, Internet singers,
and other competitors today!

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.790
This is looking like
a very high-level competition!

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:34.790
The judges will be these great
music industry professionals!

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.790
The event takes place here, at the NKP Hall!

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:42.200
What great singing
shall we experience today?

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.580
Our anticipation grows!

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.620
Maple!

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:48.950
"Fight On, Maple!!"

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:51.830
"Fight On, Maple!!"
We're here for you!

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.950
"Maple" "Fight On!!" "Fight On!!" "Maple"
Good luck!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.910
"Fight On, Maple!!"

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.660
It's almost time, but...

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.910
Where did May-<i>chan </i>go off to?

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:27.200
There she is!

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.370
May-<i>chan</i>...

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:32.000
Come on, I was looking all over for you.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.700
We have to go now, or else we won't make it.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.450
Come on, let's go.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.500
May-<i>chan</i>?

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:41.330
--No.
--Huh?

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.410
I quit. I'm not going.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:50.160
The other people are
all super popular and almost pro.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:53.790
All of the judges are editors
for music magazines,

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:57.160
famous producers, and people like that.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:00.500
I'd only make a fool of myself by joining.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.700
Wh-Where are you going, May-<i>chan</i>?!

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:06.080
Home. I don't want to go
out of my way just to look bad.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.950
What was that for?!

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.620
Wake up, May-<i>chan</i>...

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.540
May-<i>chan</i>, you're always so cool!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:34.950
But now... because you don't want
to look bad, you want to run away...

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:36.620
That's super uncool!

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.330
But... I can't...

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.410
Huh?

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:47.910
I can't show everyone
how miserable I would look!

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:55.540
Everyone... helped prepare so much!

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:59.000
They took a break from work! Cheered me on!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.580
And if I... If I...

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.790
If after all that, I don't sing well...

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:14.330
What if I can't meet everyone's expectations...?

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.290
Don't worry.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.790
Don't worry, May-<i>chan</i>.

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:27.870
Hey, remember back when
I first came to the Minaduki house?

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:35.500
I couldn't fit in, so I was crouched in
a corner of the room, and you scolded me.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:40.040
Crouching won't change anything.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.200
That's what you said as you took my hand.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:51.620
Remember what we promised then?

00:19:54.200 --> 00:20:00.000
Can I always be by your side, Maple-<i>chan</i>?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:05.620
So that, in the future, when you are in trouble,

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.160
I can be there to help you!

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.580
So, May-<i>chan</i>.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.950
If you're afraid, I'll give you a hand.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:23.750
Crouching won't change anything.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.910
Cinnamon...

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.580
Face forward.

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.620
Contestant number 22...

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.370
...Miss Maple Minaduki.

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.660
Congratulations on winning the prize!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.330
Thanks, everyone!

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.580
I'm glad you got that guitar.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:12.660
Yes.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:16.250
Now, starting tomorrow,
I can practice to my heart's content!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.830
Hey.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.200
Sing something.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.450
What?!

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:21.950
Yeah, good.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:23.700
I want to hear! I want to hear!

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:26.500
B-But you can't all of a sudden...

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.330
May-<i>chan</i>.

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.950
I want to hear, too.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.250
Fine, then.

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:37.200
As a thanks for your support, here's a song.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.450
Sing, May-<i>chan</i>...

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:21.870
"Illustration by Yuuki Hagure"
"Please Watch Again!"
